responses.response:
I'm trying to teach myself to have nicer handwriting. Can you help?

\documentclass{article}

\usepackage{tikz}

\begin{document}

\begin{tikzpicture}
\node[anchor=south] (letter) at (0,0) {A};
\end{tikzpicture}

\end{document}


This is what I get:

I would like to have it look more like this:

• You can add the option [draw] to the node. – TeXnician Jun 24 '17 at 16:50
• I think it's better to add [draw] as an option to \begin{tikzpicture}. – egreg Jun 24 '17 at 16:50
• I'm not sure that it's the same font, but you can draw the letter by hand using TikZ and the [draw] option as suggested by TeXnician. – egreg Jun 24 '17 at 16:52
• @egreg -- The font is the same; the OP has simply not enabled the border around the letter. – Steven B. Segletes Jun 24 '17 at 16:54
• @StevenB.Segletes Yes, I know, but the letter in the example is a bit wider. – egreg Jun 24 '17 at 16:55

If you want to draw the letter A, then you can use the following code:

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tikz}

\begin{document}

\begin{tikzpicture}
\node[draw] (letter) at (0,0) {A};
\end{tikzpicture}

\end{document}


This is the output:

If you want to use a different font, you can use the fontspec package with the appropriate option.
